{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-17T10:29:59.329Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 4. Summary of the work:\n\n**Implementation (3 source files + 1 wiring change):**\n- `src/watcher/autopilot.ts` — the `AutopilotCommands` port and `runAutopilotPass`, which reads task 3's view, takes one step, writes/updates the change marker, applies the stop-hold rule, writes the one stop record with the mapped reason/command/detail, and logs `autopilot: ` lines.\n- `src/cli/autopilot-commands.ts` — builds the port from `planCommand`, `approveCommand`, `landCommand` with no-op writers and test seams.\n- `src/watcher/loop.ts` — `runWatcherOnce`/`startWatcher` run the pass after every cycle when the port is given and autopilot is enabled; `--once` keeps cycling while a step was taken; `runWatcherCycle` untouched.\n- `src/cli/watch-service.ts` — `runWatcher` hands `createAutopilotCommands` to `startWatcher`.\n\n**Tests (2 new files):**\n- `tests/autopilot-run-support.ts` — temporary git project with the three-item queue, planner adapters, and a recording port, reusing recovery-support helpers.\n- `tests/autopilot-run.test.ts` — 9 tests, one per scenario.\n\n**Verification:** task verify passes 9/9, and `pnpm verify` exits 0 (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint). Result written to `.run/results/4.md`.\n\nTouched: src/watcher/autopilot.ts, src/watcher/loop.ts, src/cli/autopilot-commands.ts, src/cli/watch-service.ts, tests/autopilot-run.test.ts, tests/autopilot-run-support.ts"}}
